   172	```
   173	
   174	- `getBySession` returns an empty array for a session with no records, never `undefined`, so a caller can total the results without a null check ([validated by: returns empty array for unknown session](../../src/infrastructure/stores/inMemoryUsageStore.test.ts#L31)).
   175	- `getBySession` returns only the records of the session asked for, in the order they were recorded ([validated by: filters by session ID](../../src/infrastructure/stores/inMemoryUsageStore.test.ts#L35)).
   176	
   177	### PromptBuilderConfig
   178	
   179	Configures static system prompt assembly. Provide your AI identity, domain context, response guidelines, and custom instructions. The `PromptBuilder` combines these with tool instructions from the registry into the final system prompt.
   180	
   181	<!-- doc-block: src/infrastructure/builders/promptBuilder.ts#PromptBuilderConfig -->
   182	
   183	```typescript
   184	interface PromptBuilderConfig {
   185	  identity: string;
   186	  domainContext?: string;
   187	  responseGuidelines?: string;
   188	  toolPreamble?: string;
   189	}
   190	```
   191	
   192	`toolPreamble` overrides the built-in instructions that tell the model when to reach for a tool; leave it unset to keep the default.
   193	
   194	### OrchestratorHooks
   195	
   196	Async lifecycle hooks for customizing the orchestration flow. Every hook is optional and receives the current session, and an orchestrator built with none behaves exactly as one built with an empty set ([validated by: works without any hooks configured](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L380)). Install hooks through `HalEngineConfig.orchestrator.hooks`; `createHalEngine` forwards the set to the orchestrator ([validated by: forwards an orchestrator hook, so one passed through the config actually fires](../../src/config.test.ts#L19)).
   197	
   198	<!-- doc-block: src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#OrchestratorHooks -->
   199	
   200	```typescript
   201	interface OrchestratorHooks {
   202	  beforeSession?: (session: ChatSession) => Promise<void>;
   203	  afterSession?: (session: ChatSession) => Promise<void>;
   204	  beforeUserInput?: (session: ChatSession, userMessage: string) => Promise<string>;
   205	  afterUserInput?: (session: ChatSession, userMessage: string) => Promise<void>;
   206	  beforeModelResponse?: (session: ChatSession, systemPrompt: string) => Promise<string>;
   207	  afterModelResponse?: (session: ChatSession, responseText: string, usage?: UsageMetadata) => Promise<void>;
   208	  onError?: (session: ChatSession, error: Error) => Promise<void>;
   209	  /** The supported seam for an EU AI Act Art. 14 human-oversight control: fires before each known tool's executor, and a returned ToolResponse replaces the call (see docs/adding-a-tool.md); it receives the model's raw tool input and, through session, the caller's authHeaders, so a policy that logs either logs personal data and credential material; the engine asserts nothing about any policy installed here. */
   210	  beforeToolCall?: (session: ChatSession, call: ToolCall) => Promise<ToolResponse | undefined>;
   211	  /** Fires when the model asks for a tool round the budget refuses, after the last provider call and before afterModelResponse; a returned string reaches the user as the turn's closing text, and the engine writes none of its own (see specs/hal-engine-tool-budget/spec.md). */
   212	  onToolBudgetExhausted?: (session: ChatSession, budget: ToolBudgetInfo) => Promise<string | undefined>;
   213	}
   214	```
   215	
   216	The hooks fire in this order:
   217	
   218	```
   219	beforeSession → beforeUserInput → afterUserInput → beforeModelResponse → ...streaming (beforeToolCall × each tool call, each round)... → onToolBudgetExhausted (only on an exhausted budget) → afterModelResponse → afterSession
   220	```
   221	
   222	- The order above holds for a successful pass ([validated by: calls all hooks in correct order](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L307)).
   223	- When the stream fails, `afterModelResponse` is skipped and the tail becomes `onError` then `afterSession` ([validated by: error path calls onError then afterSession](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L347)).
   224	- `beforeSession` runs before any other hook ([validated by: called before anything else](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L106)).
   225	- `beforeUserInput` receives the content of the last user message ([validated by: receives the last user message content](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L168)).
   226	- `beforeUserInput` can modify that message by returning a different string ([validated by: modifies user message when returning different value](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L183)).
   227	- `afterUserInput` receives the message as `beforeUserInput` left it, not as the client sent it ([validated by: receives user message after any beforeUserInput modification](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L198)).
   228	- `beforeModelResponse` can replace the system prompt, for example loading it from a `PromptStore` ([validated by: replaces system prompt with returned value](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L215)).
   229	- `afterModelResponse` receives the collected response text and the usage the provider reported ([validated by: receives collected response text and usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L230)).
   230	- `afterModelResponse` does not run when the stream throws, so it never reports a response that was not delivered ([validated by: not called when stream throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L250)).
   231	- `onError` receives the session and the error ([validated by: called with session and error when stream fails](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L272)).
   232	- `onError` observes rather than handles: the error still propagates to the caller after it returns ([validated by: error still propagates after onError hook](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L294)).
   233	- `onToolBudgetExhausted` fires only when the model asks for a tool round the budget refuses: after the last provider call and before `afterModelResponse`, which then receives the hook's sentence at the end of the response text ([validated by: hands afterModelResponse text ending in the sentence, and the usage of a run without the hook](../../src/orchestration/toolBudget.test.ts#L214)).
   234	- `afterSession` runs after everything else completes ([validated by: called after everything completes](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L139)).
   235	- `afterSession` fires even on error ([validated by: called even when an error occurs](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L149)).
   236	
   237	A hook receives the full `session` object, so it has access to `session.authHeaders?.authorization` (the caller's bearer token forwarded from the WebSocket upgrade request) and every user message verbatim through `session.entries`; the engine redacts nothing before calling a hook. Anything a hook persists becomes the deployer's own data-retention obligation.
   238	
   239	## Message Lifecycle
   240	
   241	Here is what happens from the moment a user hits "send" to the moment they see a response streaming in:
   242	
   243	```mermaid
   244	sequenceDiagram
   245	    participant U as User
   246	    participant CC as Client
   247	    participant WS as WebSocket
   248	    participant S as Server
   249	    participant CO as chatOrchestrator
   250	    participant AI as AI Provider
   251	
   252	    U->>CC: types message, hits send
   253	    CC->>WS: sendMessage(content)
   254	    Note over WS: Creates optimistic entry<br/>(shown immediately)
   255	    WS->>S: {type: "user_message", content}
   256	
   257	    S->>S: validateMessage()
   258	    S->>S: createUserEntry(), appendEntry()
   259	    S->>WS: {type: "entry_upsert", index: 0, entry: UserEntry}
   260	

